cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to Stemsyl, please cite it as below."
title: "Stemsyl: a colour-stem phonetic script for English, with keyboards for phones and watches"
abstract: >-
  Stemsyl is a phonetic writing system for English in which each syllable is a short horizontal stem carrying up to
  three vertical ticks (the consonant before the vowel, the vowel, and the consonant after it). A tick's position (up,
  centred across the stem, or down) and its colour name exactly one sound: 24 consonants as eight colour families of
  three, and 14 vowels as seven colours in up to three positions. Because each sound is a position and then a colour,
  Stemsyl can be typed with two taps on a 3 x 3 grid of keys. This release contains the specification (a defensive
  publication, dedicated to the public domain), free reference apps for phones and watches, and a 271,173-word
  pronouncing list.
type: software
